parseFloat is operation
parseFloat purpose "Read text as a Float64 as `refined run` reads it into an address: 0 when it is a number, 1 when it is not, 2 when it is too large for a Float64; the value stored is 0 unless it is read: refined_parse_float"
parseFloat invariant readsCorrectlyRounded "\"Accepts `-`? digits (`.` digits)? ([eE] [+-]? digits)? only, and reads it as the nearest Float64, ties to even; past the largest Float64 is too large, below the smallest rounds to zero\""
